      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Critics argue that the focus on harm prevention and public perception can lead to self-censorship, and that this approach can stifle honest, uncomfortable, and intellectually necessary debate. Advocates for a platform that hosts real political debate suggest a more unabashedly free-speech-based approach, reserving intervention only for explicit, actionable threats of harm. This approach prioritizes open discourse and intellectual exploration, even if it means tolerating some degree of discomfort or offense.",
